  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "yhhnxv0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Psychology is defined as the scientific study of mind, brain, and human behavior.",
        "Wilhelm Wundt established the first psychological laboratory in Leipzig in 1879, founding experimental psychology.",
        "Learning theories are broadly categorized into Behaviorism (Pavlov, Skinner) and Cognitive/Constructivist models (Piaget, Vygotsky).",
        "Memory operates through three key stages: Encoding, Storage, and Retrieval.",
        "Maslow’s Hierarchy of Needs structures human motivation from basic physiological needs up to self-actualization."
      ],
      "id": "8rkpfje"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
