      "id": "38p2ppl"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q6vsl2v",
      "content": "Psychology is the scientific study of human behavior and mental processes. In nursing practice, understanding psychology helps nurses communicate effectively with patients, understand emotional responses to illness, and provide holistic care. In nursing competitive exams such as RRB Nursing, questions often come from learning, memory, intelligence, personality, emotions, motivation, and psychological development."
    },
